  "audit" = {
      "label" = "R502 WSG camp chain fold audit",
      "comment" = "The WSG camp-chain fold, the fourth seam round after gap closure: no new book pages, the R499 pattern applied to the camp chapter. One campsite flows through six landed headers: the rest quality and Table 38 fire (rules/wsg/wsgfire.h R474: the three fire sizes, the fuel ladder 6, 12, 18 turns for an eight-hour burn, the refuel ladder 3, 6, 9, the wind resistance 20, 30, 40, the rest penalties 1, 1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 4 hours, the plate economy 5-to-1 and 9-to-5), the fire starting and fuel rules (rules/wsg/wsgfuel.h R475: the 15 mph breeze bar, the 30 mph no-start maximum, the 2d20/3d20 start dice, the 3-turn small-fire grace, the capacity doubling 6 at 10 feet to 12 at 20), the wildfire rules (rules/wsg/wsgblaze.h R476: the spark carry 10, 20, 30 feet plus one foot per mph of wind, the growth ladder 1, 2, 4 turns, the 6-turn uncontrollable bar, the halving divisor), the tent quality system (rules/wsg/wsgsleep.h R473: the pole ladder 2, 4, 6, the 10 mph leak step with the 5 mph leak, the 25 percent damage chance), the natural shelters (rules/wsg/wsgshelter.h R471: the 3-turn material floor, the 6-turn lash) and the R499 temperature chain re-read for the seam. The findings: the uncontrollable bar of 6 turns is exactly one hour; the small-fire refuel interval and the grace period are the same 3 turns in two headers; the 20 mph wind value appears in three headers; the no-start maximum equals the medium fire wind resistance; the growth ladder is the only geometric ladder; the rest cold threshold is the R499 below-0 boundary and the rest hot threshold of 90 opens one degree past the protected no-damage top of 89; and the plate economy loses a flat 4 hours either way.",
